.SH NAME
STRIP860 - Strips symbol information from object files.
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
\&\fBstrip860\fR\fR\& [ \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& ] \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\
\& ... 
.SH ARGUMENTS 
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the target iPSC\*R/860\fR\fR\fR\fR\
\& object file. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You may specify the following \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& in any order:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-l\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Strip line number information only.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-x\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do not strip static or external information. (Not implemented)
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-b\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do not strip static, external, or scope information. (Not implemented)
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-r\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do not strip static, external, or relocation information.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-V\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the tool banner (tool name, version, etc.).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
Use \fBstrip860\fR\fR\& to strip symbol information from object files. 
.LP
The default is to strip all symbols. This is generally only acceptable for executables.
.SH SEE ALSO
.LP
\fBas860\fR\fR\&, \fBar860\fR\fR\&, \fBdump860\fR\fR\&, \fBicc\fR\fR\
\&, \fBif77\fR\fR\&, \fBld860\fR\fR\&, \fBnm860\fR\fR\&, \fBsize860\fR\fR\
\& 
.LP
\fR\fR
.LP
